---
const questions = [
  {
    q: 'What do I need on the machine?',
    a: 'A Linux or macOS machine with OpenSSH Server enabled. On macOS that is System Settings &gt; General &gt; Sharing &gt; Remote Login. Node is optional and only used by encrypted notifications.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens to the terminal I already had open?',
    a: 'Attach and Reattach use Herden takeover mode, disconnecting the previous terminal owner when necessary.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where did the Host runtime come from?',
    a: 'It is an Apache-2.0 derivative of pristine upstream herdrdev/herdr. Herden is maintained independently by 3LOC and records the exact upstream baseline in the repository.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where can I read the design decisions?',
    a: 'In <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/3loc/herden/tree/main/docs/adr"><span class="mono">docs/adr/</span></a>. The transport story in particular is not obvious.',
  },
];
---

<section id="faq" class="section">
  <div class="container layout">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">FAQ</div>
      <h2 class="heading">Before you install</h2>
    </div>
    <dl class="list">
      {
        questions.map((item) => (
          <div class="row">
            <dt class="question">{item.q}</dt>
            <dd class="answer" set:html={item.a} />
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 320px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 80px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .heading {
    font: var(--type-h2);
    font-size: clamp(24px, 4.4vw, var(--fs-h2));
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-heading);
    margin-top: var(--sp-4);
  }

  .list {
    margin: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .row {
    padding: 28px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .question {
    font: var(--type-h5);
  }

  .answer {
    font: var(--type-body-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin: var(--sp-2) 0 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 40px;
    }
  }
</style>
